nodecode-rea is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins
  commit 1690b63a4790cb821fb6a319ba524815d4e09411
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's `mcp.json` — the pinned `npx -y rea-agents@6.7.0 mcp`
server, its stdio transport, and the two environment variables it forwarded
(`REA_GHIDRA_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_MS`, `REA_PWNTOOLS_PYTHON`) — as a cell that
launches the server itself and exposes it as two model tools and the verbs
`rea:tools`, `rea:schema`, `rea:call`, `rea:status` and `rea:restart`, so no
`mcp.servers` entry is hand-written. Also rewritten: the
`skills/reverse-engineer-anything` and `skills/crash-triage` workflows, as
the prose `(help :rea)` answers.

Left out: the two skill folders verbatim and their six reference documents
(the workflow is condensed to the primer, not shipped as files); the
`REA_KUNA_COMMAND`, `REA_TSHARK_COMMAND`, `REA_CAPINFOS_COMMAND`,
`REA_SIGROK_COMMAND` and `REA_WABT_BIN_DIRECTORY` environment variables,
which the plugin did not forward either — engines are found on PATH as REA's
own default; the `crash-triage` helper script, a standard-library Python file
whose job the crash tools now do through the same server; and the plugin's
per-server call budget, which is the cell's `call_timeout_seconds` setting.
